// ui: create an app on the ui package and build or run it on the web, macOS, iOS or Android.
//
//   eskiuc tools/ui/main.esk -o ~/.eskiu/bin/ui   # install (any directory on the PATH)
//   ui new myapp                                 # a project that depends on ui
//   cd myapp && ui run ios                       # web | macos | ios | android
//   ui serve                                     # build again and reload on each change
//
// Inside a project, the ui package is the one eskiu.lock names; its hosts (hosts/) are built
// around the app. Yoga, for the native hosts, is fetched and compiled once into
// $ESKIU_HOME/cache. Its parts: common, config (ui.toml), project, web, macos, yoga, ios, android, gradle (Maven dependencies), xcode (Swift packages), new, serve, agent (`ui agent`, the driver's client), uitest (`ui test`), diagnostics (--json), publish (`ui publish`, with src/apis/ed25519.esk).
